jobs.description:
We offer the opportunity to work across a broad range of accounting activities as part of a dynamic and professional team, within an attorney-oriented firm culture that emphasizes quality, continuous improvement, and high performance. You will report directly to the Finance Manager, also based in Brussels. As Accountant, you will manage the full range of general ledger operations, including encoding, day-to-day bookkeeping, closing procedures, and VAT, across 3 legal entities, ensuring accurate and complete records are delivered on time and in full compliance with legal and tax obligations.

Main responsibilities

• Prepare and record monthly journal entries and adjustments, including supporting documentation and appropriate descriptions;
• Daily follow up of the banks accounts and reconciliation with the General Ledger;
• Prepare VAT returns and the Intra-community listing;
• Prepare monthly reconciliation of  the general ledger accounts;
• Enter Cash receipt on a daily basis;
• Backup for the Payables Team;
• Support the Senior Accountant in the monthly closing activities and in the Balance Sheet reconciliation. 
• A Bachelor degree in Belgian accounting (or equivalent);
• Experience with accounting principles, Belgian VAT and payroll reconciliation; 
• Experience with an Enterprise Resource Planning software;  
• Excellent command of English and French or Dutch; 
• Pro-active work attitude, results-oriented, rigorous and flexible;
• Excellent analytical and communication skills (both orally and in writing);
• Strong  knowledge of MS office and Excel in particular (VLookup, Pivot table, ...);
• Ability to perform effectively in a service-oriented environment and demonstrating professional ethic and manner;
• Ability to work independently while at the same time showing a true team spirit.

For our client in VEURNE, we are looking for an INDUSTRIAL ELECTRICIAN.

Our client is a well-known company in Veurne, responsible for electrical projects from A to Z.

As an INDUSTRIAL ELECTRICIAN in VEURNE, your responsibilities include:

• Installing electrical installations in the residential and industrial sectors;
• Connecting electrical cabinets;
• Laying cables, chasing and cutting;
• Carrying out work based on plans and bills of quantities;
• Managing a team of 2–3 people;
• Executing projects from A to Z.
As an INDUSTRIAL ELECTRICIAN in OSTEND, you recognize yourself in the following:

• You have relevant experience as an industrial and/or residential electrician;
• You hold a Category B driving licence;
• Physical work is not a problem for you;
• You speak Dutch, English, or French.

For our client in the Veurne region, we are looking for a SOLAR PANEL TECHNICIAN.

Our client is a well-established company with years of experience in providing sustainable energy solutions. With a strong passion for technology and technical installations, they are committed to helping build a greener future. Would you like to contribute to the transition towards renewable energy in Belgium and neighboring countries? Then keep reading!

As a SOLAR PANEL TECHNICIAN in the Veurne region, your responsibilities will include:

• Connecting solar panel installations, home battery systems, and/or EV charging stations;
• Installing the inverter and providing the required AC and DC cabling according to industry standards;
• Connecting the AC and DC cables to the inverter;
• Making any necessary modifications to the electrical distribution board;
• Completing the single-line electrical diagram to ensure the technical inspection can be carried out;
• Commissioning the complete installation and providing the customer with clear instructions and explanations on its operation.


As a SOLAR PANEL TECHNICIAN, you recognize yourself in the following profile:

• You hold a valid Category B driving licence;
• You have a strong electrical background (experience with solar panels is an advantage but can be taught);
• You are able to read and interpret technical drawings with ease;
• You speak Dutch or English;
• You have a strong focus on safety and always follow the correct procedures and regulations.

For our client located in Bredene, we are looking for a CNC TURNER.

As a CNC TURNER in the Bredene region, you will perform the following tasks:

• You will sometimes produce small series of parts, while other times you will make unique, customer-specific pieces;
• You will work on a wide range of components, from large rollers and large-diameter parts to wear sleeves for pumps and parts for combine harvesters;
• You will start with smaller pieces and gradually grow into working on larger components;
• To work efficiently, you can read and understand technical drawings;
• You manufacture unique parts based on technical drawings, with little repetitive series work;
• You accurately measure and check finished products.
As a CNC TURNER in the BREDENE region, you can identify with the following:

• You have experience as a conventional turner, milling machine operator or CNC turner? Great, we are looking for you!
• We have approximately 25 machines. You will not have a fixed workstation but will learn to operate almost all of them. You will start on a standard lathe and gradually develop your skills;
• You can read and understand technical drawings;
• You speak Dutch or English.
